# dropnode fact sheet

## domain

- a Node is a labeled rectangle on the Canvas with a unique id, a position, and dimensions; its label content dictates a minimum width (GraphNode in code)
- a Group is a distinct kind of node (kind 'group') that visually and logically contains child nodes via their parentId; nesting is one level deep — a Group never contains another Group
- a Connection is a directed curve linking a Handle on a source Node to a Handle on a target Node, identified by its four endpoint fields
- a Handle is a connection anchor on one of the four edges of a Node (top, right, bottom, left); its position is derived from the Node's rect
- a Resize Grip is a draggable control at one of the four corners of the selected node, used to change the node's size; distinct from a Handle
- the Canvas is the unbounded workspace containing all Nodes and Connections
- the Viewport is the visible region of the Canvas, defined by a pan offset and a zoom scale
- the Graph State is the complete serializable model: the arrays of all Nodes and all Connections, and nothing else
- a Command is an undoable user action exposing execute(), undo(), and a description
- the History is the ordered record of executed Commands, split into an undo stack and a redo stack
- the Snap Zone is a 30-canvas-unit radius around a Handle; a dragged connection endpoint inside it attaches to that Handle
- a Node owns exactly four Handles, one per edge; a Group carries the same four Handles
- deleting a Node cascade-deletes every Connection referencing it as source or target
- all Graph State lives in GraphService signals; components mutate it only through the service, transient drags directly and undoable actions via Commands
- Import replaces the Graph State wholesale after validation; Export serializes it to JSON

## nodes

- double-clicking empty Canvas creates a Node labeled "New Node" centered on the cursor, as a single undo step
- new Nodes default to 160x48; after render the measured label width (120px floor) raises the Node's width but never shrinks it — manual sizes are grow-only protected
- Node auto-sizing updates go directly to GraphService and never create a History entry
- four Resize Grips show at the corners of the selected node only; dragging one resizes with the opposite corner anchored
- a grip drag clamps width to the label-derived minimum (max of 120 and the measured label width) and height to 48
- an entire grip drag is one undo step: per-mousemove size updates bypass History, and a single ResizeNodeCommand is pushed on mouseup only if the rect changed more than 2px
- double-clicking a Node opens inline label editing; Enter or blur commits, Escape cancels; empty or unchanged labels are never committed
- renaming a Node is undoable and restores the exact previous label
- deleting an unknown Node id throws "Node {id} not found"; deleting an unknown Connection id is a silent no-op
- Node ids follow the pattern node_{timestamp}_{counter} and Connection ids conn_{timestamp}_{counter}; the counter is monotonic within a session

## groups

- the toolbar "Add Group" button creates a 320x200 Group labeled "New Group" centered in the Viewport, as a single undo step; Groups use the node_ id pattern
- membership is containment, judged by the node's center point on mouseup: center inside a Group's bounds joins it, center outside releases it — each change is one undo step
- when overlapping Groups both contain the drop point, the topmost-rendered Group (later in the nodes array) claims the node
- dropping a node into a Group it is connected to succeeds and severs those Connections: move, membership change, and severed Connections form one compound undo step restoring original ids
- dragging a Group moves it and all its children rigidly as one undo step; children keep absolute Canvas coordinates (ADR-0005)
- dragging a child inside its Group only moves the child; membership is unchanged
- deleting a Group releases its children in place (un-parented, positions kept) and removes the Group's own Connections as one compound undo step; undo restores membership and Connections with original ids
- a Group cannot be connected to its own children in either direction: createConnection returns null, connection drags never snap to the counterpart, and Import rejects such payloads
- a Group can be resized no smaller than its children's bounding box plus 16 canvas units of padding; a childless Group clamps to the same 120x48 floor as a Node; resize never changes membership
- label: double-clicking a Group's label strip edits its label inline; double-clicking its body creates a "New Node" child at the cursor as one undo step
  command: grep -q 'createChild' src/app/components/node/node.ts
- Groups render beneath regular nodes and draw their fill at 30% alpha so children stay visible

## colors

- label: the palette holds exactly 8 curated colors (NODE_PALETTE); an absent color field means the default node background
  command: grep -q 'NODE_PALETTE' src/app/models/node.ts
- a swatch row (default + 8 palette colors) appears in the toolbar center only while a node is selected; clicking a swatch is one undoable SetNodeColorCommand, and re-clicking the active swatch is a no-op
- Import rejects color values outside the palette wholesale with "Invalid node {id}: color must be a palette color"

## connections

- dragging from a Handle rejects self-connections and exact duplicates silently (createConnection returns null); reverse-direction and different-handle pairs between the same two Nodes are allowed
- label: during a connection drag, a dragged endpoint snaps to the nearest Handle within a 30-canvas-unit Snap Zone; the snapped Handle highlights
  command: grep -q 'snapThreshold = 30' src/app/components/connection-layer/connection-layer.ts
- the source Node's own Handles are never snap targets during a connection drag
- dropping a connection drag in empty space (no snap) creates nothing
- during a connection drag a dashed ghost bezier renders from the source Handle to the cursor
- clicking a Connection path or its Label selects the Connection; Delete or Backspace deletes the selected Connection as one undoable Command
- selection is exclusive: at most one element (Node or Connection) is selected at a time — selecting one kind deselects the other, and clicking empty Canvas or pressing Escape clears whichever is selected
- a Connection carries an optional Label; double-clicking the path or Label opens inline editing at the curve midpoint — Enter or blur commits, Escape cancels, and committing empty removes the Label (deliberate deviation from the Node rule)
- setting or clearing a Connection Label is one undoable SetConnectionLabelCommand; committing unchanged text pushes nothing onto History; createConnection never sets a label
- a Connection Label renders as horizontal text on an opaque pill centered at the cubic bezier midpoint, moving with the curve; the pill is part of the Connection's hit area
- Connections render as cubic beziers; control points extend perpendicular to each Handle's edge, offset clamped between 40 and 150 (distance x 0.4)
- Handle positions are the midpoints of the Node's four edges, computed from x, y, width, height

## viewport

- zoom is clamped to the range 0.1 to 5
- wheel zoom steps by 0.1 per tick, centered on the cursor so the point under the cursor stays fixed on screen
- toolbar zoom buttons step by 0.1 centered at origin (0,0), not at the screen center — this differs from wheel zoom
- mousedown-drag on empty Canvas pans the Viewport and deselects the current Node
- reset view restores pan (0,0) and zoom 1; importing or clearing a graph does NOT reset the Viewport
- pan and zoom apply as one shared CSS translate+scale transform covering both the DOM node layer and the SVG connection layer

## history

- Ctrl+Z undoes and Ctrl+Shift+Z redoes; there is no Ctrl+Y binding
- executing or pushing any new Command clears the redo stack
- undo and redo on empty stacks are silent no-ops; the stacks have no size limit
- an entire Node drag is one undo step: per-mousemove position updates bypass History, and a single Command is pushed on mouseup only if movement exceeded 2px in either axis — a MoveNodeCommand normally, a compound when the drop also changed Group membership, a MoveGroupCommand for Group drags
- a plain click on a Node selects it without creating a History entry
- deleting a Node via Delete/Backspace removes the Node and its Connections as one compound undo step; undo restores the Node and its Connections with their original ids
- Import does not clear History, so undoing after an Import can reference stale ids
- switching between Projects (or to the Scratch Canvas) clears History — undo never crosses a Project boundary

## import-export

- Import is validate-then-replace: an invalid payload is rejected wholesale with a specific error message and existing state stays untouched
- Import validation rejects duplicate Node ids, Connections referencing Nodes absent from the same payload, and handle values outside top/right/bottom/left; an empty graph is valid
- Import validation also rejects kind values other than 'group', off-palette colors, parentId values that reference a missing node or a non-Group, Groups carrying a parentId, and Connections linking a Group to its own child
- payloads without kind, parentId, or color import unchanged as plain nodes — pre-Group exports and links stay valid
- Import validation does NOT reject duplicate Connection ids or self-connections — only createConnection guards those
- a Connection label field, when present, must be a string or the payload is rejected with "Invalid connection {id}: label must be a string"; empty-string labels import cleanly and render as no Label, and payloads without label fields import unchanged
- label: the Export menu offers four items — Export JSON file, Copy JSON, Copy link, and a disabled Export to Drive placeholder hinting "Sign in required — coming soon"; it opens from the Scratch Canvas toolbar and from each project row's Export submenu in the Sidebar
  command: grep -q 'Export to Drive' src/app/components/toolbar/toolbar.ts && grep -q 'Export to Drive' src/app/components/sidebar/sidebar.ts
- label: Export downloads pretty-printed 2-space JSON named dropnode-graph.json with a success toast; Copy JSON copies the same JSON to the clipboard with a success/error toast
  command: grep -q 'dropnode-graph.json' src/app/services/export.service.ts
- a project row's Export actions read the stored graph from localStorage and never navigate; the file is named after the Project (slugged), falling back to project.json
- Copy link copies <origin>/?data=<url-encoded pretty JSON>, dropping any existing path and query parameters — share links always land on the Scratch Canvas; the link is copied whatever its length, with a success/error toast
- the Export menu is built on @angular/cdk/menu primitives; export side effects live in ExportService, never in the toolbar component
- exported Graph State is a copy; mutating it does not affect editor state
- label: on startup the app imports a Graph State from the URL query parameter named data; ?data is honored only on the Scratch Canvas route (/), never on /p/:projectId; a missing parameter is a silent no-op
  command: grep -q "params.get('data')" src/app/services/graph.service.ts
- invalid URL data shows an error toast prefixed "URL data invalid: "; a successful URL load toasts "Graph loaded from URL"
- the import dialog offers File Upload and Paste JSON tabs; file content takes precedence over pasted text, errors show inline and keep the dialog open

## collections

- a Collection is a named container of zero or more Projects shown as a parent entry in the Sidebar; Collections are flat — never nested
- every Project belongs to exactly one Collection; a Project is a saved graph with its own route /p/:projectId
- label: Collections and Projects — including each Project's Graph State and Viewport — persist in localStorage under the single schema-versioned key dropnode:collections (ADR-0007)
  command: grep -q "dropnode:collections" src/app/services/collection.service.ts
- Collection ids follow col_{timestamp}_{counter} and Project ids proj_{timestamp}_{counter}; duplicate Collection and Project names are allowed
- / redirects to the most recently opened Project; a ?data share link or an empty store stays on the Scratch Canvas
- an unknown or deleted /p/:projectId redirects to / with a "Project not found" error toast
- editing auto-saves: Graph State and Viewport changes persist to the current Project debounced at 300ms; there is no save button and no dirty state
- the per-Project Viewport is stored outside Graph State — exported JSON and ?data links carry nodes and connections only
- deleting a Collection cascade-deletes all its Projects; Collection and Project deletion are permanent (not undoable) and both guarded by a confirmation modal, the Collection modal stating its project count
- deleting the Project being viewed navigates to the most recently opened surviving Project, or to / when none remain
- Sidebar inline rename follows the node-label contract: Enter or blur commits, Escape cancels, empty or unchanged names are never committed; newly created Collections and Projects drop straight into rename
- "Import collection" (beside "New collection" in the Sidebar header) appends a brand-new Collection from the envelope file after validating every project graph wholesale — one bad project rejects the file; collection and project ids are regenerated so importing twice yields two independent copies
- collection export downloads <collection-slug>.dropnode-collection.json containing { name, projects: [{ name, graph }] } where graph is exactly the Graph State export shape
- Import on a project row navigates to that Project first, then opens the import dialog — a replace always happens on-screen
- the toolbar shows Import, Export, and Save-as-project only on the Scratch Canvas route; on /p/:projectId those actions live on the Sidebar row menus
- "Save as project" lists Collections in a dropdown and is disabled with a "Create a collection first" hint while no Collection exists
- the Scratch Canvas survives in-session navigation in memory only — a reload still clears it; "Save as project" consumes it
- label: per-Collection expand/collapse state persists under dropnode:sidebar-collapsed-collections
  command: grep -q "dropnode:sidebar-collapsed-collections" src/app/services/sidebar.service.ts

## shortcuts

- all keyboard shortcuts are ignored while focus is in an input, textarea, or contenteditable element
- Delete or Backspace deletes the selected element — a Connection alone, or a Node with its Connections; Escape deselects and blurs the active element

## ui

- a single toast shows at bottom-right; a new toast replaces the current one and resets the 4-second auto-dismiss timer

## architecture

- Nodes are DOM Angular components and Connections an SVG overlay, per ADR-0001 hybrid rendering
- rendering stacks in three layers inside the shared transform per ADR-0008: Group cards, then the SVG connection layer, then regular node cards — Connections are clickable over Group rects but stay occluded under regular node cards
- label: the perf-critical components (canvas, node, connection-layer) use OnPush change detection per ADR-0003
  command: grep -q OnPush src/app/components/canvas/canvas.ts && grep -q OnPush src/app/components/node/node.ts && grep -q OnPush src/app/components/connection-layer/connection-layer.ts
- the root App and Toast components do not declare OnPush, deviating from the ADR-0003 mandate that all components use OnPush
- the performance target is 200 Nodes with ~100 Connections; beyond that requires virtualization or canvas rendering (ADR-0003)
- label: built on Angular 22 standalone components with signals
  command: grep -q '"@angular/core": "^22' package.json
- label: change detection runs with zone.js; the app is not zoneless
  command: grep -q '"zone.js"' package.json
- label: the unit test suite (Vitest + jsdom) passes
  command: npx vitest run --reporter=dot
- the SVG connection layer sizes itself to the node extent plus 1000, with a 5000-unit minimum
